# The size budgets for PureMouse.app (installed) and the release dmg, checked by scripts/check-size.sh
# (release.sh runs it on both, so CI does).
# Raising one is a reviewed change: say in the pull request what grew and why.
#
# Each budget is the measured size plus 15%, rounded up to the next 0.1 MB (1 MB = 1,000,000
# bytes), plus the allowance below while there is one (none after a release is measured), and the
# README's Download row quotes the measured sizes rounded to 0.1 MB. A test
# (scripts/tests/test_size.zsh) holds the budgets and the README to the measurements, so
# changing one of them means changing the measurement here.
#
# Measured 2026-11-03 from the published 0.5.1 release: `PureMouse-0.5.1.dmg` as downloaded from
# GitHub (its SHA256SUMS checked), and the universal PureMouse.app inside it, mounted read-only and
# summed as check-size.sh sums it. The installed figure sums the bytes of every path, so the nested
# apps' hard-linked Assets.car (one inode, three names) counts three times; only the dmg holds it
# once (`du` puts the same app at 8.6 MB).
INSTALLED_MEASURED_BYTES=12429914
DMG_MEASURED_BYTES=4948496
#
# Allowance for mouse v2 (#149), cleared when 0.6.0 is measured. A budget is the measured size plus
# 15%, rounded up to 0.1 MB, plus an allowance when a change in flight takes CI's largest figure
# past that: the overshoot rounded up to 0.1 MB, so the cap keeps under 0.1 MB of headroom over what
# CI measures. The figures are CI's on 6ea7319, the larger of its two jobs (the test job's release
# dry run, and the compatibility job's Xcode 26 universal build, which is the larger installed).
# Main 43dcb6f measured 13,946,142 installed (compatibility) and 5,541,062 dmg (test); the branch
# 14,516,018 (+569,876) and 5,813,199 (+272,137). The growth is code: the device card, the app page
# and the other Settings panes (about 0.5 MB in the Settings helper, 0.05 MB in the menu bar app,
# local Swift 6.4 builds against main), plus the eight device PDFs (37 KB, in the Settings helper
# only, never in the daemon, the menu bar app or Assets.car). The hit geometry compiled from them is
# about 20 KB a slice. test_size.zsh holds the arithmetic.
INSTALLED_CI_BYTES=14516018
DMG_CI_BYTES=5813199
INSTALLED_EXTRA_BYTES=300000
DMG_EXTRA_BYTES=200000
INSTALLED_MAX_BYTES=14600000
DMG_MAX_BYTES=5900000
